GEMV tile — vector reaches the PUs through the GLOBAL BUFFER
  fill    copy (bank DRAM -> GB)
  pu_mask = gb_mc_mask  0xFFFF   (16 banks participate)
  L = 32 beats,  K = 512,  weights at DRAM row 100,  A_c,b[k] = 1 + 16c + b,  v[k] = 1
  copy    vector at bank 0 DRAM row 200, route[0]=16 (GB)
          NOTE: 2 channels, so the vector is written to bank 0 row 200 of EACH of them.
          A multicast COPY makes every channel read its OWN bank, so a shared vector
          must be replicated first.  WRVEC needs one GPR write and no replication.
  result  GPR word 1041

  programs — one per fill path.  TWO SEPARATE DOORBELLS, not one
  program: a GEMV needs exactly one GB fill and these are two ways
  of doing it.  Everything after word 0 is identical, which is what
  makes the lane comparison a test of the fill path alone.

